    state_dict before: ['conv1.weight', 'conv1.bias', 'conv2.weight', 'conv2.bias', 'fc.weight']
    state_dict after : ['conv1_channel_scale', 'conv1.weight', 'conv1.bias', 'conv2.weight', 'conv2.bias', 'fc.weight']

    conv1_channel_scale = [0.5257 0.416  0.5548 0.4144 0.6578 0.6243 0.4454 0.5737]
    register_buffer is the whole mechanism: state_dict() serializes buffers as well as
    parameters, so anything registered as a buffer is exported for free. Use it when a
    value is cheap to compute in Python and awkward to express as TensorRT layers.
