Input ->DataType.FLOAT, (1, 1, 4, 4), (1, 1, 4, 4), x
Output->DataType.FLOAT, (1, 8, 4, 4), (1, 8, 4, 4), (Unnamed Layer* 0) [Convolution]_output
    bias handed to TensorRT : [-0.1522  0.2273 -0.0047  0.2171]
    array overwritten with  : 999.0, before build()
    engine actually computed: [999. 999. 999. 999.]
    engine took the overwritten values: True

    trt.Weights wraps a pointer. It does not copy at add_convolution_nd() time and it
    does not keep the object alive -- the values are read when the engine is built.
    Mutating or freeing the array in between silently changes the engine, and letting
    it be garbage collected is a use-after-free with no error message. Every
    hand-built network needs a keep-alive list; see `keep_alive` in the case above.
